        "text": "## Coverage\n\n| Input | END marker (quoted) | Fact near the end |\n|---|---|---|\n| INPUT-1 plan | `END-INPUT-1-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Closeout is `spec_delta_closeout.v1` / `no_spec_delta`; surfaces `.github/workflows/` and `docs/hardening-readiness.md`; evidence `plans/evidence/v2/GUARD.json`; `metadata_only`; downstream `none`. |\n| INPUT-2 receipt | `END-INPUT-2-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Post-round-6 change: plain `pnpm test` strips DB enablement/connection vars even when pre-set; only admitted launchers enable DB collection; fresh current-input review required. |\n| INPUT-3 appendix | `END-INPUT-3-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Coordinator: no build/SQL/publish this turn; process suites spread `process.env`; no package-test zero-edge assertion; existing ownership still needs amendment before unowned fixes. |\n\nSource sections **S1\u2013S9 all present** (`END-S1` \u2026 `END-S9`). Final bundle marker present: `END-BUNDLE-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d`. Historical audit corpus is **not** supplied; only this amendment plus bounded facts. Correlation `GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d`. Prior Fable/Grok results are not inherited.\n\nPlan digest `80aa9de48cde9764dd7dad66db1ce31e471fa61b2c2d5f1e55ab0e62e49bd537` matches the receipt. Roadmap `ee1f3152a5331e071042ed122e122143cc103544140a5ed8f4e849f6b649587c` matches. CASE-HY-6\u2019s three `import type { OmnigentProviderMode }` edges match S3\u2013S5, the literal scan, and S2. S6 still packs via `pnpm pack`; S7\u2019s first 50 lines always pack; those are SL-0 edits, not current proof. S8 is `coordination_query_leases` `STABLE` `SECURITY DEFINER` over active leases, default `'{}'`. S9 checks finding membership only.\n\n## What holds\n\nOwned files cover the gate, workflows, SQL launcher, pack/smoke/publish helpers, `tests/guard/**`, four process suites (timeout/cleanup only), and SL-1/SL-2 evidence paths. Parent-owned plan/TRIAGE records stay outside lanes. SQL admission, role attributes (`guard_client` `NOINHERIT` / no `BYPASSRLS`; `service_role` probe closed in `finally`), env scrub including `PGHOSTADDR`/`PGSERVICEFILE`/`PGPASSFILE`/`PGOPTIONS`/`PGSSLMODE`, pre-collection DB exclusion, fail-on-empty/skipped required IDs, tested-vs-published SHA/digest/tarball identity, no `pull_request_target`, `guard-required` fail-propagation, and the recording-only allowlist plus external before/after binding are specified. Hosted OIDC/registry success is correctly left to SHIP. DATA/COORD/WIRE/INTEG/PREP/SHIP defects are not GUARD blockers. Do not run GUARD implementation tests as a condition of this plan review.\n\n## Findings\n\n**P1 \u2014 Hosted destructive-fixture topology is not executable as written.** Destructive setup must run in verify on separate disposable instances, never the admitted fixture, including hosted PR proof. Hosted topology is one workflow PostgreSQL service plus \u201cno additional launcher/workflow paths,\u201d with Docker admitted only locally. Privilege/role/migration falsifiers on that same cluster can mutate the admitted fixture (roles, `BYPASSRLS`, objects). Name the hosted mechanism in SL-0: extra instances via the owned launcher (Docker on hosted Ubuntu, if that is the topology) **or** an equivalent isolated instance, and require those case IDs in hosted `pnpm verify`. Until that is explicit, EC-GUARD-1/2 hosted proof can be skipped, mocked, or run against the shared service while still \u201cfollowing\u201d the plan.\n\n**P2 \u2014 Impl constraints without test bullets.** Signature-only resolve of `coordination_acquire_lease(jsonb)` (never execute) and the read-only `coordination_query_leases('{}'::jsonb)` probe are impl text only. Add required-case falsifiers: missing acquire fails admission; lookup is `pg_proc`/equivalent; invoke counts stay zero; probe transaction is read-only.\n\n**P3 \u2014 Unnamed enablement and dispatch controls.** Hostile `pnpm test` stripping needs a frozen enablement-variable name. Real vs dry-run `workflow_dispatch` needs a named default-false input. Otherwise ambient-enable and mode-routing tests have no stable identity.\n\n**P4 \u2014 Non-blocking.** Validator \u201cunmatched\u201d semicolon interface is unexplained (`bounded child helper` looks provided but unconsumed). Closeout `no_doc_delta` vs SL-1 README/`docs/hardening-readiness.md` is already decided, not a new gate. S7 is truncated; do not treat it as full smoke semantics. Receipt `status=pending_amendment_review` is intentional; only allowlisted fields plus an external digest binding may change after reconciliation.\n\nRound-6 ambient-`pnpm test` hole is closed. No IF is produced here.\n\nPARTIALLY AGREE\n",
