        "text": "| Input | Coverage and quoted END marker | Specific fact near the end |\n|---|---|---|\n| INPUT-1 | Complete supplied plan; `END-INPUT-1-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Spec closeout declares `no_spec_delta` and `metadata_only`. |\n| INPUT-2 | Complete supplied pending receipt; `END-INPUT-2-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Migration inspection records no database execution and limits acquire-function inspection to its signature. |\n| INPUT-3 | Complete supplied bounded appendix; `END-INPUT-3-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` | Closing observations identify four process suites spreading `process.env`; the source scans explicitly do not establish AST enforcement. |\n\nSource sections S1 through S9 are present, with `END-S1`, `END-S2`, `END-S3`, `END-S4`, `END-S5`, `END-S6`, `END-S7`, `END-S8`, and `END-S9`. `END-SOURCE-EVIDENCE` and the final marker `END-BUNDLE-GUARD-REVIEW-c858e97ceaf64896adca16158b714f7d` are present. This review covers the amendment and bounded source evidence, not the full historical audit corpus.\n\nNo blocking or material corrective finding is established by the supplied candidate.\n\n- **Ownership is sufficient for the proposed work.** SL-0 includes the existing publishing helper, transport smoke, workflow files, configuration and process suites it must change. The three import exceptions match S2\u2013S5 and remain narrowly assigned to PREP for repair. Tooling changes do not authorize unrelated production fixes.\n- **SQL admission and privilege requirements are coherent.** Fixture ownership, inherited environment removal, installer admission, constrained client identity and dedicated role-switching probe form a concrete setup contract. S8 supports the proposed query probe, while the plan correctly limits its evidentiary value: a SECURITY DEFINER query does not establish caller RLS behavior or hosted Supabase correctness. Real positive and negative setup controls remain SL-0 obligations.\n- **Artifact identity covers the tested-to-published path.** The amendment directly addresses S6\u2019s existing repacking behavior and S7\u2019s internally packed smoke input. Retained tarballs, event-derived source identity, producer-bound artifact selection and digest checks connect verification, smoke, rehearsal and publication. The E404 stub control addresses the gap left by rehearsals that only encounter already-published versions; actual OIDC and registry acceptance remain SHIP evidence.\n- **Failure propagation and test selection are explicit.** Stage failures, signal/null exits, suppressed DB collection, missing required case IDs and unsuccessful verification dependencies have specified falsifiers. The latest amendment also makes plain `pnpm test` exclude DB collection despite hostile inherited enablement. Worker isolation addresses the source-observed environment propagation without requiring unowned process-suite rewrites.\n- **The recording-only acceptance procedure is sound as written.** External before/after digests avoid a self-referential receipt hash. The path allowlist is constrained by unchanged reviewed inputs, explicit decisions and the material-change rule. Historical runner state remains separate, and accepting TRIAGE cannot produce GUARD acceptance.\n\nThe remaining implementation tests, hosted checks and protection observations are scheduled evidence obligations, not reasons to reject this plan amendment before implementation. The pending receipt is intentional. This review supplies one fresh independent assessment; it does not establish the other seats\u2019 results or coordinator acceptance.\n\nAGREE",
